# Supabase setup
# 1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com/dashboard.
# 2. In that project, open Project Settings > API.
# 3. Copy the Project URL into NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL below.
# 4. Copy the "Publishable key" into NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY.
#
# Create a local .env.local file beside this file, then copy these two values
# into it. Next.js reads .env.local automatically when you run `pnpm dev`.
# Do not commit .env.local or paste real keys into this .env.example file.
#
# Both values below are intentionally public: they are used by the browser.
# Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) must protect database access. Never put a
# Supabase service_role/secret key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable or browser code.
#
# Before enabling Google sign-in later, configure the redirect URL in Supabase:
# Authentication > URL Configuration > Redirect URLs
# - Local development: http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
# - Production: https://your-domain.com/auth/callback

# Example: https://abcdefghijklmnop.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Example: sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
